    feat(semantic): read a generic component at its default instantiation

    ADR 0026 S5. A generic component's props parameter has its type
    parameters open, so Poly<E extends ElementType = "div"> had two props
    where <Poly /> has every attribute of a div. The checker API cannot
    instantiate a signature, so the instantiation is written as source: one
    file held in the checker's memory (createSnapshot's fileSystem layer,
    read by tsrs 0.23 and the Go 7.1 beta) declares
    Parameters<typeof Poly<"div">>[0] for each generic component whose first
    type parameter declares a default, in a second snapshot made only when
    one was requested. A line the checker reports an error on keeps the
    component's structural props, with the instantiation and the error as
    the reason. Gate: Poly<"div"> 281 props, Poly<"a"> 289, on both checkers;
    the checker lane now runs it on tsrs.

